            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "On October 18, 2017, the FBI mistakenly raided a family home in suburban Atlanta belonging to Curtrina\u202fMartin and others instead of the intended target."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioners argue that the statutory proviso should be applied more broadly."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioners contend that the Eleventh Circuit\u2019s interpretation of the discretionary\u2011function exception would eliminate most of the Federal Tort Claims Act and the liability the proviso was intended to provide."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the FTCA does not permit the Eleventh Circuit\u2019s Supremacy Clause defense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the Eleventh Circuit must assess the issue without reference to its mistaken view that the law\u2011enforcement proviso applies to subsection (a)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8933bf7d996b-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court concluded that decisions such as In\u202fre\u202fNeagle do not create a judicial or legislative immunity defense."
      }
